 ## Background
-The method is based on the volume rendering integral, discretized into a summation [S3, unofficial]. It was introduced by Marc Levoy in 1990 [S2, S4]. The specific analysis of sampling strategies and boundary artifacts was conducted in the Inviwo visualization framework, supported by ELLIIT, SeRC, and VINNOVA grants [S3, unofficial]. The technique is a fundamental approach in direct volume rendering, often contrasted with indirect methods like ray marching with acceleration structures or ray tracing [S2, unofficial].
